  "status": "shared-native-source-catalogue-and-result-owner-verified-in-stages",
  "scope": [
    "CompositionNodeMemory holds the fixed 512 MiB Node allowance. A render creates one owner before load and passes it through native ingestion/catalogue, export result/RPC/replay reservations and concurrent source revalidation. Finally closes that owner; standalone result-only callers preserve the old scope.",
    "Native catalogue capacity is admitted before transport/catalogue/variant construction. Walk schema-validated source data without JSON/geometry copies; count unique normalized authored overrides, eight full source trees for transport/schema/hash staging and four per-variant metadata trees. Source1/3 share static mesh data; source2 fully parsed pose geometry is charged per variant.",
    "Grow existing ingestion reservations without releasing their capacity first. Preserve larger conservative lexical admission for escaped sources. Only completed preparation transfers its reservation to a shared owner; failure/cancellation closes local reservations while preserving other owners.",
    "Result transient release also drops its private control record. Six new unit controls include combined quota denial, uninterrupted admission, failure cleanup, shared mesh sizing, 9,000 transient retirements and escaped-source admission; two new filesystem controls exercise actual source3 coexistence/failed verification and cancellation during actual catalogue hashing."
  ],
  "qualification": "Current fast15/Node16 and actual PBR composition/normal/mixed plus all six native2 groups pass on unchanged inputs15. The render Node metrics are shared-ledger snapshots (before final publication validation), not complete lifetime/process-RSS measurements. Root composition file/text/serialization, other media/code-identity producers, aggregate world/body/replay, final full milestone gates and installed refresh remain separate. Direct producers that do not pass a shared owner retain their original result-only scope; standalone preparation snapshots cover its producer before caller handoff. No quota increase, rendered-math change, whole-Node completion, human acceptance or publication is claimed.",
